> One problem with it that jumps out immediately is that names must end in
> consonants.  I don't have a word list handy, and I'm not fluent, so I can't
> say any more about this possibility.  Good luck.

Words that end in consonants must be names, but the converse is not
true.  Any brivla can be used as a name, so {la vlananla} is quite
acceptable (if unpronouncible).

